=== README.md
     1	# relay
     2	
     3	A small service that reads messages from standard input and forwards each one to an upstream endpoint, with a
     4	bounded work queue, a worker pool and retries. In this checkout the upstream is simulated by printing the
     5	request to standard output.
     6	
     7	## Running
     8	
     9	    cp config.example.properties config.properties
    10	    java tools/RunTests.java                       # compiles into build/classes first
    11	    java -cp build/classes com.acme.relay.Main config.properties < messages.txt
    12	
    13	Without an argument the service reads `config.properties` from the working directory.
    14	
    15	## Configuration
    16	
    17	| Key                  | Required | Default | Meaning                                                     |
    18	|----------------------|----------|---------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
    19	| `upstream.url`       | yes      |         | URL the messages are forwarded to                           |
    20	| `api.token`          | yes      |         | Token sent to the upstream                                  |
    21	| `worker.threads`     | no       | `4`     | Number of delivery threads, at least 1                      |
    22	| `queue.capacity`     | no       | `1000`  | Messages waiting for a free worker, at least 1              |
    23	| `retry.max-attempts` | no       | `3`     | Retries after the first failed delivery, 0 or more          |
    24	| `request.timeout`    | no       | `30s`   | Time limit per delivery: a whole number plus `ms`, `s`, `m` |
    25	| `metrics.enabled`    | no       | `false` | `true` or `false`: print delivery counts on shutdown        |
    26	
    27	## Tests
    28	
    29	    java tools/RunTests.java
    30	
    31	The runner compiles `src/main/java` and `src/test/java` and runs every JUnit 5 test. It needs
    32	`lib/junit-platform-console-standalone.jar`.
